      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coach's verdict",
          "heading": "Fernandez says Italy create chances but lack finishing before Fiji test",
          "body": "Italy breakdown coach German Fernandez remains confident in the squad despite defeats by South Africa and Argentina, saying Italy keep creating chances but lack finishing — and that the players have the quality to fix it. Reviewing the 14-19 loss in Genoa, he noted Argentina were down to 13 men after two yellow cards and said Italy had no truly easy penalty kicks. Ahead of Saturday's Fiji test, he warned against losing attacking ball to a side that thrives in chaos."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand's Quinn Tupaea needs thumb surgery, out 10 weeks",
