    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-17",
      "edition": "Tuesday 17 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Fly-half rankings",
          "heading": "Planet Rugby ranks 'most accomplished' Finn Russell among world's top 10 fly-halves",
          "body": "Planet Rugby's November list of the world's best No. 10s bills Scotland fly-half Finn Russell as 'most accomplished', though it places a rival it labels the 'greatest player' above him. The verdict follows a mixed afternoon for Russell in Sunday's 15-12 win over Australia at Murrayfield. He hit the post with an early conversion and was beaten in the tackle for Harry Potter's first-half try. He then landed the 75th-minute penalty that gave Scotland breathing space before Saturday's meeting with Japan."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand's Quinn Tupaea needs thumb surgery, out 10 weeks",
          "body": "Ireland's Jamie Osborne ruled out with pectoral injury."
