      }
    },
    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-17",
      "edition": "Tuesday 17 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Player reaction",
          "heading": "Eddie James calls Wales' All Blacks win 'best day of my life'",
          "body": "Wales centre James, 24, made 25 tackles and scored one of Wales' five tries in Saturday's 35-28 win over New Zealand, admitting afterwards he could barely feel his feet. His tackle stopping Anton Lienert-Brown just short of the line was among the defining moments. With only 55,152 at the Principality Stadium, he wants the win to draw more supporters for Australia's visit: \"The more fans we have, the louder it is.\" Of 139 fans in the app who answered after full-time, 99% were buzzing."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand's Quinn Tupaea needs thumb surgery, out 10 weeks",
          "body": "Ireland's Jamie Osborne ruled out with pectoral injury."
        }
