      }
    },
    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-17",
      "edition": "Tuesday 17 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "French verdict",
          "heading": "Midi Olympique warns Pumas must raise game to avoid Paris thrashing",
          "body": "Midi Olympique journalist Jérôme Prévôt was unimpressed by last weekend's 19-14 win over Italy in Genoa. He called it a narrow victory over a truly mediocre Italian side and a disappointing rough draft that Argentina must improve on against France in Paris to avoid a thrashing. He noted that the penalty count finished 16-16 and that the Pumas trailed until the 38th minute. Italy fly-half Paolo Garbisi then kicked a late penalty dead with the hosts still able to win."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand's Quinn Tupaea needs thumb surgery, out 10 weeks",
          "body": "Ireland's Jamie Osborne ruled out with pectoral injury."
        }
      ],
