      }
    },
    "461": {
      "date": "2026-11-17",
      "edition": "Tuesday 17 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "World Cup clock",
          "heading": "Les Kiss sees 'every chance' of Wallabies improvement before home World Cup",
          "body": "Grilled in Edinburgh on whether time remains before next October's home World Cup in Perth, Wallabies head coach Les Kiss said he was happy with it. \"I do think there's every chance that there will be improvement,\" he said after Sunday's 12-15 loss to Scotland, a fourth straight defeat. Next is an attack reboot before Wales in Cardiff, after the Wallabies' lowest points total in 15 Tests; captain Harry Wilson conceded it \"probably didn't get to where we would have liked to be.\""
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand's Quinn Tupaea needs thumb surgery, out 10 weeks",
          "body": "Ireland's Jamie Osborne ruled out with pectoral injury."
        }
      ]
    },
    "463": {
      "date": "2026-11-17",
      "edition": "Tuesday 17 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Bold vow",
          "heading": "Eddie Jones' 'play the house down' vow ends in 13-try Twickenham hiding",
          "body": "Japan head coach Eddie Jones promised before last Saturday's Nations Championship match against England that his side would \"play the house down.\" What followed at Allianz Stadium was a 15-78 defeat in which England ran in 13 tries, five of them by England's Will Joseph. Writing for the Guardian, Gerard Meagher said the Brave Blossoms \"looked like Sunday afternoon amateurs.\" The loss leaves Japan tenth of 12 in the log with one win from five going into the Round 6 meeting with Scotland."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand's Quinn Tupaea needs thumb surgery, out 10 weeks",
          "body": "Ireland's Jamie Osborne ruled out with pectoral injury."
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "name": "Japan Today"
      }
    },
    "465": {
      "date": "2026-11-17",
      "edition": "Tuesday 17 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Rennie says All Blacks 'let the country down' as Tupaea faces surgery",
          "body": "Outside centre Quinn Tupaea, a fixture in the All Blacks' side throughout 2026, needs surgery on a thumb injury and will miss the next 10 weeks, ruling him out of Saturday's test against England at Twickenham. Head coach Dave Rennie, demanding a reaction after the 35-28 loss to Wales, said of his players: \"They know we let ourselves down and we let the country down.\" Rennie is set to recall a host of big names, and star wing Will Jordan is in the selection mix after a hamstring problem."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland's Jamie Osborne ruled out with pectoral injury",
          "body": ""
        }
      ],
      "match": {
        "venue": "Allianz Stadium, Twickenham"
      },
      "source": {
        "name": "BBC Rugby Union"
      }
    },
    "467": {
      "date": "2026-11-17",
      "edition": "Tuesday 17 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Officiating row",
          "heading": "Rassie Erasmus asks if unpunished knee-drops in France defeat amount to match-fixing",
          "body": "Speaking in Dublin on Monday, Springbok head coach Rassie Erasmus claimed 17 knee-drop tackles went unpenalised in Friday's 19-21 defeat by France. \"If he saw it and decided not to act on it, is that not match-fixing?\" he asked of the TMO, before insisting it was not an accusation. He also predicted Ireland fly-half Sam Prendergast, cited for a hip-drop tackle against Fiji, would escape a ban on a technicality for Saturday's test. Of the 43 fans in the app who answered after the France result, 63% were fuming."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand's Quinn Tupaea needs thumb surgery, out 10 weeks",
          "body": "Ireland's Jamie Osborne ruled out with pectoral injury."
